Z||000004||BBBAD GT||08-28-2000||01:26 PM||||Loki:  Unfortunately, most people ask me what that other Stang was doing passing me like that.  It was a trailered/striped/race only car, that I believe was pushed to the starting line.  It was a procharged 302, that broke about the 1000' mark, thats why you see me coming up on him pretty darn fast in the end.  I drove 100 miles to the track, put slick on, ran the piss out of it, then drove back home.  I'm happy with that.  Here is the timeslip if you want <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/TimeSlip.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/TimeSlip.jpg</A> <BR>The motor in the Fiero is a stock roller longblock 350.<P>Zorba:  I'm actually changing the gauges this winter.  Its just a piece of alum Chris made  so he could put some 2" gauges where the tach was.  I'm going with Autometer speedo/tach in the original holes, and putting Autometer electrical oil pres/water temp/amp gauges in the stock pod gauge where the tach is sitting now.  Should hopefully look like Batboys setup.  The gauges in it now are just the std autogauge units, and VDO tach.<P> <BR>||||reg||1
